// GIO's streams (ginputstream.h, goutputstream.h, gfilterinputstream.h,
// gfilteroutputstream.h, gmemoryinputstream.h, gmemoryoutputstream.h,
// gpollableinputstream.h, gpollableoutputstream.h, gpollableutils.h,
// giostream.h's streams of a GIOStream, gsimpleiostream.h), as GIO runs
// them: a stream is closed once, one operation at a time ("Stream has
// outstanding operation"), the cancellable of a synchronous call is the
// thread's current one while it runs, and an asynchronous call's
// callback is wrapped so the pending mark is gone when it runs.
//
// The default asynchronous operations are GIO's: a pollable stream
// (GPollableInputStream that can poll) is read without blocking and
// waited on with its source when it would block; any other stream's
// synchronous operation runs in a thread of its own (a GTask). Closing
// and flushing asynchronously run the synchronous ones at once and
// report from the task (GIO runs them in a thread; the result and its
// moment, a later iteration of the main context, are the same).
//
// The instances: a GInputStream is a GObject and (24) a record of
// closed (0), pending (4) and the outstanding callback (8); a
// GOutputStream's record has closed (0), closing (4), pending (8) and the
// outstanding callback (16). A GFilterInputStream or GFilterOutputStream
// adds its base stream (32) and keeps whether closing it closes the base
// in its instance private data. The socket streams of a GSocketConnection
// (GSocketInputStream, GSocketOutputStream) add their socket (32). A
// pollable source is a GSource (96 bytes) and its stream (96).
const m = @import("./memory.mlx")
const threads = @import("./threads.mlx")
const errors = @import("./errors.mlx")
const messages = @import("./messages.mlx")
const types = @import("./types.mlx")
const ioerrors = @import("./ioerrors.mlx")
const cancellable = @import("./cancellable.mlx")

